{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.gwu.edu/": {
      "title": "Home",
      "description": "Careers at GW | Human Resource Management & Development | The George Washington University Skip to main content Careers The George Washington University FIND A POSITION Main Bootstrap Navigation Our Community Our Benefits Our Opportunities Our Community Our Benefits Our Opportunities Home Why GW? George Washington envisioned a university that would educate future generations of citizen-leaders and serve as an intellectual hub for the country. Since then, the George Washington University (GW) has evolved into a top research institution and the largest institution of higher education in Washington, D.C.  Located in the heart of the nation’s capital, working at GW offers you unique experiences associated with our strategic location and culture, in addition to generous tuition and retirement benefits. Today, thousands of people from more than 130 countries come to take full advantage of GW’s vast network of world-class academic, research, and employment opportunities. We are a diverse and inclusive community, and we believe that every role and every person at GW contributes to our collective success and pursuit of excellence.  We seek people driven to put their knowledge to work for an immediate impact on the world. If this sounds like you, welcome to GW. Image Image \"We are training people in all kinds of fields, whether it is in the government or security or something else. So that means that the people we are shaping with our curriculum are then out there, shaping the industries. We are shaping a variety of industries, just in the work we do here. That’s incredible. \" Cody House Director of Online Learning and Instructional Technology, College of Professional Studies 3,700+ Full and part-time staff 3 Campuses situated around Washington D.C. 1,500+ Faculty Our Community Our culture is focused on nurturing talent and helping our students and employees alike realize their full potential. Become part of a community committed to helping each other in everyday life as we strive to make history. Our Benefits Take advantage of a wide variety of benefits designed to support each stage of your career and improve your—and your loved one’s—quality of life. Our Opportunities People come to GW to make their mark on the world. Explore the myriad ways in which you can help advance discovery, convene and collaborate with influential figures and shape the course of the nation. Staff Profiles: “Have You Met…” As a vital component of the university's mission, the contributions of staff are visible throughout the campus. From academic departments, building operations, groundskeeping, athletics, student support, and campus living, staff play a crucial role in supporting all aspects of our university community. “Have You Met…” is a tribute to our staff, celebrating their achievements, sharing their stories, and acknowledging their impact. See what our staff has been up to below! GW Careers Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Flr Washington, D.C. 20006 202-994-8500 askhrmd gwu [dot] edu (askhrmd[at]gwu[dot]edu) Student Positions Faculty & Library Positions Staff Positions Research Positions Resources for Prospective Employees Frequently Asked Questions Campus Advisories EO/Nondiscrimination Policy Website Privacy Notice Contact GW Accessibility Terms of Use Copyright Report a Barrier to Accessibility"
    },
    "https://careers.gwu.edu/our-opportunities": {
      "title": "Our Opportunities",
      "description": "Our Opportunities | Careers at GW | Human Resource Management & Development | The George Washington University Skip to main content Careers The George Washington University FIND A POSITION Main Bootstrap Navigation Our Community Our Benefits Our Opportunities Our Community Our Benefits Our Opportunities Home Our Opportunities Our Opportunities Move your career forward at GW With ten schools and numerous other academic and administrative areas, George Washington offers a wealth of rewarding career opportunities. Our community includes thousands of talented and dedicated staff that each play a vital role in shaping our citizen-future leaders, utilizing Washington, D.C. as an extended classroom unlike any university, hosting the world’s most influential leaders, supporting groundbreaking research and shaping policy that changes the world. GW is always looking for talented, ethical, compassionate and energetic people who are excited by the opportunity to shape ideas, individuals and even institutions. If you think you would be a perfect fit for our community, we’d like to hear from you. Career Development to Support Your GW Journey Whatever path your career takes at GW, we are here to support your journey. We know that our most important resource is our world-class education. With our Tuition Remission program, employees have access to prestigious courses and degrees to support their professional development or assist with their loved ones' educational pursuits. All employees have access to LinkedIn Learning and Talent at GW, platforms with thousands of webinars and training options to develop in the skills necessary for their career - or provide an opportunity to learn something new. With our Performance Management program, guided by our Talent and Organizational Development and Compensation teams, each employee receives personalized feedback and professional development from their supervisor, helping them to continuously grow and develop. \"One of the things that I love about working here is the amount of collaboration that I get to have with both the faculty and the students. Not only that, but I also get to collaborate with a lot of simulation experts throughout the field. GW has such an incredible draw for leaders in nursing and leaders in simulation that it has helped me grow in my field, just with the ability to meet people all the time.\" Crystel Farina, PhD, RN, CNE, CHSE Associate Dean for BSN Programs Explore Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty & Librarian Opportunities Research Opportunities GW Temps Opportunities Employee Referral Bonus Program We are excited to announce the launch of the Employee Referral Bonus program! All eligible staff will receive a $1,000 bonus, subject to tax withholding, if they successfully refer a qualified candidate to fill a vacant staff or research position. Further details and information can be found on the Human Resource Management and Development (HRMD) website . Equal Employment Opportunity The George Washington University (GW) is an Equal Opportunity (EO) employer committed to maintaining a nondiscriminatory, harassment-free, diverse work and educational environment. The university does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of protected characteristics or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law in any of its programs, activities, or employment practices. For more information on this policy and its purpose, please read the Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement (PDF) . The EEOC Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal notice provides information regarding applicable laws and procedures for filing complaints if you believe these standards has been violated. GW Careers Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Flr Washington, D.C. 20006 202-994-8500 askhrmd gwu [dot] edu (askhrmd[at]gwu[dot]edu) Student Positions Faculty & Library Positions Staff Positions Research Positions Resources for Prospective Employees Frequently Asked Questions Campus Advisories EO/Nondiscrimination Policy Website Privacy Notice Contact GW Accessibility Terms of Use Copyright Report a Barrier to Accessibility"
    },
    "https://gwu-studentemployment.peopleadmin.com/": {
      "title": "GW Student EmploymentLearning in Action",
      "description": "GW Student Employment - Applicant Portal | Home Skip to Main Content GW Student Employment Learning in Action Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student User Guide Career Appointments & Events, Internships, External Jobs Research Commons Graduate Assistantships & Fellowships GW Full-Time and Part-Time Staff Messages from the Administrator When creating a new account, use your GW email account. DO NOT use your GWID. Your email address should reflect your name @gwu.edu. Do you need to know how to accept your FWS offer or download your FWS Program Statement? Check out our resource document About Your FWS Program Statement . Welcome to the Student Employment Applicant Portal! Student Employment at GW offers part-time positions that help students gain valuable experience while earning an hourly rate. Positions include Federal Work-Study (FWS) roles, available to students who receive an FWS offer as part of their financial aid, as well as non-FWS positions, which are open to domestic and international GW students. Student Employment refers only to on-campus jobs (and approved off-campus organizations for FWS). It does not include jobs through GW Human Resources, Graduate Student Assistantships or Fellowships, internships, or employment with external organizations. Use the menu on the right to learn more about those opportunities. Non-FWS On-Campus FWS Off-Campus FWS All Student Positions What is Student Employment at GW? Learn more about the FWS Program. Get help with your resume & cover letter. Assistance for GW hiring managers and supervisors. Contact Us If you have any questions, you can reach us at gwse@gwu.edu or 202-994-8046, or during drop-in hours Monday - Friday 10:00 am - 4:00 pm on the 5th floor of the Marvin Center. Follow us on Twitter and Facebook . Payments, Taxes, & Benefits Student Employees are paid on a biweekly scedule. Earnings are subject to state and federal taxes. Learn more about payment, taxes, and benefits . Types of Positions Student Employment positions are temporary part-time jobs in which the student earns an hourly wage. There are a wide variety of different positions available. Learn more about position types and functions . Equal Employment Statement The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action (EEO/AA) employer committed to maintaining a nondiscriminatory, harassment–free, diverse work and education environment. The university does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of protected characteristics or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law in any of its programs, activities, or employment practices. For more information on this policy and its purpose, please read the Equal Employment Opportunity Policy Statement . GW Student Employment Center for Career Services 800 21st St. NW Suite 505, DC 20052 Phone: (202) 994-8046, Email: gwse@gwu.edu https://careerservices.gwu.edu/student-employment Connect with us on Twitter and Facebook To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
