    "https://careers.gwu.edu/frequently-asked-questions": {
      "title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
      "description": "Frequently Asked Questions | Careers at GW | Human Resource Management & Development | The George Washington University Skip to main content Careers The George Washington University FIND A POSITION Main Bootstrap Navigation Our Community Our Benefits Our Opportunities Search Our Community Our Benefits Our Opportunities Home Frequently Asked Questions Frequently Asked Questions How do I search for jobs? Visit GW’s career website to set up your user profile, search for positions of interest and monitor the status of your application(s).  To search for positions, click the Search Jobs link on the left side of the page. We encourage you to visit our career site regularly as new opportunities are posted daily. How can I apply for a job? To apply for a job, click the Create Account link at the left side of the page, and then follow the directions to set up your personal account. Returning candidates should click on Login, and enter your username and password. This enables you to apply to new positions without re-entering your application information, and review the status of positions for which you have applied. Do I need a resume? Each posting provides information about the documents which are necessary to complete and submit your application for the position.  All postings will require you to submit a resume.  To submit your resume you will upload a Word (.doc) or PDF (.pdf) file at the attachment step of your application. Should I provide a cover letter? Each posting provides information about the documents which are necessary to complete and submit your application for the position. Most postings will require you to provide a cover letter, although for some postings it may be an optional document which you may choose to upload.  Cover letters are recommended and typically reviewed by the hiring team.  A cover letter is your opportunity for you to provide additional information about your credentials and talents that make you the best match for the position.  To include a cover letter you will upload a Word (.doc) or PDF (.pdf) file at the attachment step of your application. What else do I need to know about applying? When you submit your application online, you will immediately receive an email to confirm the receipt of your application.  If you do not receive an email notification, please check your spam folder or log in to your account to review your application submission. Once your application is received, the hiring team will have access to your application materials.  If the hiring team determines your qualifications are a match for the position, they will reach out to you by phone or email. Are non-US citizens eligible for employment at The George Washington University? We do not sponsor for employment Visa status in staffing our positions. The application will ask you if you are legally authorized to work in the United States for any employer. Am I able to make changes to my application? Once your application is submitted for consideration, it’s not possible for you to return to it to make revisions.  Please reach out to us if you would like assistance: Staff and Research Opportunities: gwujobs@gwu.edu Faculty and Librarian Opportunities: fpo_recruit@gwu.edu GW Temp Opportunities: ita@gwu.edu What types of jobs are posted on the GW Careers page? As the largest private employer in the District of Columbia, the university offers a wide variety of opportunities whether you are searching for your first, or your next, career.  These may be full-time, part-time, and limited-term positions. The posting for each position will provide detailed information about the terms, location, and typical hiring pay range for the position. Career opportunities are available in many areas: Faculty: With ten schools and colleges, GW employs full- and part-time faculty in disciplines across the board. Research: Home to traditional disciplines as well as more than eighty centers and institutes, our research spans science, technology, health, policy, global security, arts, and humanities. GW has a variety of research positions, giving employees amazing opportunities for exploration and discovery. Staff: In both part- and full-time positions, our talented staff team at GW brings together people from diverse backgrounds with a wide variety of skills and abilities to fill a broad assortment of roles. We strive to build a strong sense of community that supports service excellence across our academic programs, offices, departments, and campuses. GW Temps: As GW’s internal temporary agency, GW Temps matches applicants with temporary assignments at the university. Assignments are diverse in duties as well as in scope, lasting anywhere from one day to many months. Where can I find contact information for the hiring manager for the position? If the hiring team determines your qualifications are a match for the position, they will reach out to you by phone or email.  For a variety of reasons, including privacy protection, we do not provide hiring manager contact information. How does the application process work? The application process can be an involved one, but it's an opportunity for you to get to know GW’s values and culture – and for us to understand a little bit more about you. That's why we want to give you a few tips on what to expect because being open, honest and transparent about expectations is a big part of who we are. Learn more about GW Values which are shared by our students, faculty, and staff. They serve as a guiding force, shaping our everyday lives on campus and helping to ensure that we make the best decisions for our university community. Once your application is submitted, your materials are reviewed by the hiring team.  They will contact candidates who are a good fit for the position and who model GW’s values. As the recruitment process moves forward, the candidate status of your application will be updated.  If you are not selected for a specific position, there may be other opportunities in the future, so please continue to view our openings and apply for additional positions of interest. How can I check the status of my application(s)? To check on the status of your application(s), returning candidates should click on Login, and enter your username and password. This enables you to apply to new positions without re-entering your application information, and review the status of positions for which you have applied.  Each department within GW manages the hiring process independently so we do not have additional specifics on the status of each application that is being reviewed. Can I submit my resume/cover letter for a position without submitting an application? We do not accept resumes or cover letters which are submitted by email. To have your qualifications considered, please visit our career site .   This is where you may set up your user profile, search for positions of interest, and monitor the status of your candidacy. What if I’m not selected for an interview? If you notice your status says “not selected” there may be other opportunities in the future, so please continue to view our openings and apply for additional positions of interest. If you see that your status says “candidate withdrawn” you have opted to withdraw from consideration for this position. If this is an error, please reach out to us: Staff and Research Opportunities: gwujobs@gwu.edu Faculty and Librarian Opportunities: fpo_recruit@gwu.edu GW Temp Opportunities: ita@gwu.edu What is GW Temps? GW Temps is the internal temporary employment service at GW and is a dedicated venue for GW schools and departments to hire temporary staff. GW Temps staff enjoy many of the resources available to GW employees while gaining valuable experience to prepare for a full time career with GW. Visit the GW Temps webpage to learn more. How do I request an accommodation during the application process? If you are a qualified individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, you may request a reasonable accommodation if you are unable or limited in your ability to access job openings or to apply for a job on this site as a result of your disability. You can request reasonable accommodations by contacting The Equal Employment Office and Employee Relations by email at eeo@gwu.edu by phone at 202-994-9656, or by fax at 202-994-9658. GW Careers Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Flr Washington, D.C. 20006 202-994-8500 askhrmd@gwu.edu Student Positions Faculty & Library Positions Staff Positions Research Positions Resources for Prospective Employees Frequently Asked Questions Campus Advisories EO/Nondiscrimination Policy Website Privacy Notice Contact GW Accessibility Terms of Use Copyright Report a Barrier to Accessibility Use of personal data and cookies This site uses cookies to offer you a better browsing experience. Visit GW’s Website Privacy Notice to learn more about how GW uses cookies. Preferences Decline optional Accept all"
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128680": {
      "title": "Senior Associate Director, Venues",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Senior Associate Director, Venues Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Senior Associate Director, Venues Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: The George Washington University was founded in 1821 in response to a vision that the nation’s foremost founder spelled out in his last will and testament. He dreamed of a university that would educate the citizen leaders of the new nation he had done so much to create. Today the university that bears his name is different in many ways from what George Washington could have imagined. He could not have imagined the sheer size of its enrollment, now 26,000 students, including women as well as men from all 50 states and more than 100 countries. Nor could he have envisioned a university with multiple campuses and 14 schools; with more than 120 departments and 95 centers and institutes; with a half-million-square foot science and engineering building; with a school of public health, located on a circle that bears his name; or with a museum housing a world-class collection of textiles and the history of the great capital city he had only begun to plan. GW Venues (a department in the Division of Safety and Operations) produces and manages events in specialty venues on the Foggy Bottom Campus. We provide services to a broad spectrum of clients both in the community and outside of the community. We provide spaces for our students, faculty, staff and guests to host events, meetings and gatherings. We highlight university traditions, produce memorable guest speaker events and coordinate many other activities unique to our campus with local, national and international acclaim. Our record of excellence, support and cooperation is one that we are proud of. Reporting to the Director, Venues, the Sr. Associate Director, Venues assists with supporting the GW Venues Team that manages the logistics for events and activities booked on campus by an Event Hosts. These events provide support for both internal and external partners who require logistical assistance in specialty event venues, outdoor spaces and other emerging partner campus venues. This position serves as the strategic lead for sponsored and external events booked at the University Student Center ( USC ). The Sr. Associate Director manages two Venue Managers as direct reports to manage the events at USC and other emerging partner venues on campus. Responsibilities include: Serves as the lead Venue Manager for sponsored and external events at USC and other specialty venues on campus overseeing assigned events from the planning stage through live execution. Partner with leadership to strategically market the unique abilities and resources of the USC , actively engaging with high-value prospective clients to pitch capabilities, overcome objections, and successfully bring in new clients. Manages two Venue Managers as direct reports. Partners with event hosts to plan and execute campus events while actively enforcing all university compliance policies, safety guidelines, accessibility standards, and operational excellence expectations. Assists in the development, enforcement, and updating of venue usage policies, event safety procedures, scheduling protocols, operational guidelines, and SOPs for new venues. Contributes to weekly team meeting agendas and participates actively in cross-functional coordination meetings to align on upcoming event requirements and coordinating with USC operational staff. Ensures spaces are utilized at optimal capacity during events. Works with event hosts on logistical planning, direction, and execution, including but not limited to consulting on vendor selection, script review, and budgeting. Serves as the primary liaison between clients, contractors, caterers, administrators, and university partners to manage all logistical aspects of events. Conducts pre-event walk-throughs with clients, vendors, and security to familiarize them with the venue. Supervises event onsite, acting as the primary point of contact for troubleshooting and last-minute adjustments. Conduct post-event walkthroughs with clients to ensure the venue, furniture, and equipment are returned in their original condition, documenting any discrepancies or maintenance issues that require resolution. Coordinates and cultivates relationships with shared services and partner departments across campus (e.g., Facilities, Campus Safety, GWPD , AV, Housekeeping, USC staff, etc.) to execute event logistics, including room setup, vendor/attendee access, staffing, and crowd management to ensure all operational needs are addressed efficiently. Works with clients to determine room setups and create/update diagrams for each event. Provides guidance to clients regarding third-party vendors for additional services (e.g., décor, entertainment, rentals) and work along with the Production Team to provide guidance on vendors for additional AV services. Assists with interviewing candidates, training, and supervising venue staff. Assists with the development and management of trainings and templates for venue staff. Creates detailed event orders—including comprehensive timelines, setup logistics, furniture and equipment needs, and labor requirements—to clearly communicate operational expectations and final costs to the client. Consults with the scheduling department to assess availability for requested events and staffing needs at venues on campus. Maintains accurate records of event details, incidents, and client feedback for continuous improvement, assisting with the development, distribution, and analysis of post-event evaluation surveys. Creates and sends all appropriate reports in a timely manner. Performs other related duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. The position is based at GW’s Foggy Bottom Campus in Washington, DC. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a high school diploma/ GED plus 4 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Bachelor’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: CMP or related certification required. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working at a University is desired 4+ years’ experience organizing complex events, managing large auditoriums/theaters or TV quality studio venues is preferred. PERSONAL CHARACTERISTICS This position desires an individual with the following characteristics: Commitment to GW’s values Intellectual, professional and a person of integrity Honest, with the highest ethical standards Passionate, collaborative, strategic, and smart with a hands-on, roll-up-the-sleeves orientation Ability to work independently Self-starter; hard worker Takes the initiative; very high energy Personally accountable Assumes ownership, control, and accountability for all areas of responsibility and commitments made to others Sincere, open, and direct communicator Puts organizational interests above self-interests and is comfortable expressing candid opinions Highest levels of responsiveness Combination of strong intellect that is combined with a practical and realistic common sense understanding of how to get things done Ability to demonstrate initiative, a strong desire to succeed and exert the extraordinary effort often required Ability to work in a fast-paced, high-growth, entrepreneurial environment Ability to work with faculty and staff in a respectful way Establish trust and credibility with institutional leadership and across the University Seeks “win-win” solutions to help foster continued integration and collaboration Flexible and receptive to change A positive “can-do” attitude. Hiring Range $76,921.10 - $133,924.98 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Division of Safety and Operation Family Safety and Facilities Sub-Family Events Stream Management Level Level 1 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:30 am - 5 pm, with flexibility to work occasional nights and/or weekends Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014429 Job Open Date: 08/26/2026 Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)?  (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your expected salary range? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/124846": {
      "title": "George Washington Employment Site",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Open rank faculty positions in Ophthalmology (Comprehensive) Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Open rank faculty positions in Ophthalmology (Comprehensive) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. You will also be asked to provide the contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin on April 22, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002590 Academic Title: Open rank faculty positions in Ophthalmology (Comprehensive) Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Comprehensive Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 07/01/26-6/30/27 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates, an independent non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University, is seeking to fill full-time faculty positions in Comprehensive Ophthalmology. The Department of Ophthalmology is part of a growing academic health center located in the heart of a world-class, vibrant metropolitan area, with its cultural, family, and educational opportunities. Appointment rank (Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Full Professor) and salary will be commensurate with experience. Expected to start as early as summer 2026. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include delivering excellent patient care, teaching residents and medical students, and conducting high-quality research. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in Ophthalmology, and eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia and Virginia at the time of appointment. Advertised Salary: $250,000 - $375,000 Other Benefits: Compensation and Benefits: Will include a competitive and comprehensive package including Malpractice/Tail Coverage, 401k matching, Medical, Dental, & Vision, Disability & Life Insurance. Other Information: Will include a competitive and comprehensive package with Malpractice/Tail Coverage, 401 (k) matching, Medical, Dental, & Vision, and Disability & Life Insurance. More details can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. You will also be asked to provide the contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin on April 22, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: http://smhs.gwu.edu/ophthalmology/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/124471 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board certified or eligible in Ophthalmology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia and Virginia at the time of appointment? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128843": {
      "title": "George Washington Employment Site",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Principal Equal Opportunity Investigator Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Principal Equal Opportunity Investigator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Posting Details I. JOB OVERVIEW Job Description Summary: The George Washington University (GW) is committed to maintaining a positive climate for study and work, in which all individuals are judged solely on relevant factors, such as skill and performance, and can pursue their activities in an environment free from discrimination, harassment, and violence. The Office of Equal Opportunity supports this commitment by offering complaint resolution options, support to individuals involved in incidents, and educational opportunities designed to prevent incidents and to encourage prompt reporting. The Principal Equal Opportunity Investigator, conducts investigations into reported discrimination and harassment based on a protected characteristic, with a special emphasis on cases involving identity-based discrimination and retaliation. In addition, the Principal Equal Opportunity Investigator facilitates informal resolutions which are voluntary, remedies-based and rooted in restorative justice principles. The Principal Equal Opportunity Investigator reports directly to the Director of Complaint Resolution. Job Duties The Principal Equal Opportunity Investigator, is responsible for the following: Serving as a key partner in ensuring GW’s compliance with federal, state, and local anti-discrimination laws. Conducting prompt, reliable and impartial investigations, including the development of investigation plans, drafting notices of allegation and other essential correspondence, identifying and interviewing witnesses, gathering evidence and data, conducting site visits as needed, keeping accurate and thorough records and notes of the investigation process, applying GW policies and preparing detailed investigation reports, which may include analysis and recommendations as appropriate. Providing leadership and support to the Lead Equal Opportunity & Title IX Investigators and the Equal Opportunity investigators in the area of Title VI, VII , and IX discrimination and enforcement of the university’s Equal Opportunity, Non-Discrimination, Anti-Harassment and Non-Retaliation Policy, Title IX Sexual Harassment & Related Conduct Policy, and the Prohibited Relationships with Students Policy. This includes, among other responsibilities, leading weekly case review meetings and serving as a first level of review of investigator work product (formal complaints, investigation notices, investigation reports, negotiated resolution agreements etc.). Assisting the Director of Complaint Resolution with the development and implementation of policy and procedural improvements related to complaint resolutions. In the absence of the Director of Complaint Resolution or as otherwise needed, representing OEO at various campus/community stakeholder meetings, such as EO Case Review meetings, Threat Assessment meetings, and the DMV Title IX Administrator Working Group meetings. Facilitating impartial informal resolutions, rooted in restorative justice principles, that are aimed at identifying the harms experienced and identifying actions that can be taken to acknowledge harm, prevent its recurrence, and address its effects. Communicating with students, faculty, and staff in. a clear and compassionate manner. This may include explaining complex processes in a digestible manner, as well as providing timely updates regarding resolution processes. Collaborating with appropriate university offices during resolution processes to provide a coordinated response and holistic support. Maintaining an impartial and neutral approach and appropriate level of privacy throughout the process. Engaging in required training to ensure that skills and knowledge are current. Leading training programs for faculty, staff, and students on topics related to discrimination and harassment based on a protected characteristics. Assisting the Response team by providing supportive measures as needed when caseloads are high. The position is based at GW’s Foggy Bottom Campus in Washington, DC but may require travel to GW’s campuses in Mount Vernon, DC and Ashburn, VA and to surrounding areas. Performs other work duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning tasks logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified candidates will hold a Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area of specialization plus 7 years of relevant professional experience, or, a Master’s degree or higher in a relevant area of study plus 5 years of relevant professional experience. Degree must be conferred by the start date of the position. Degree requirements may be substituted with an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Additional Required Licenses/Certifications/Posting Specific Minimum Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Juris Doctor (J.D.) degree preferred. At least 5 years experience investigating and resolving discrimination/harassment complaints is preferred. Other comparable experience may serve as a substitute for investigatory experience (i.e. litigation experience, HR investigatory experience). Prior experience working in a higher education environment. Exceptional analytical and writing skills. Demonstrated expertise in applying relevant federal, state, and local laws desired. Strong communication and organizational skills. Familiarity with Title VI, Title VII , Title IX, VAWA , the DC Human Rights Act, the Clery Act, and FERPA desired. Experience working in union and non-union environments desired. Experience leading and providing support to other investigators. Familiarity with the concept of restorative justice. Experience with public speaking and ability to facilitate training sessions for university community members. Ability to manage and work with conflict, including meeting with individuals who may be experiencing high levels of stress. Ability to work independently, efficiently, and to balance a workload. Ability and desire to work actively, collaboratively, and creatively, as part of a team. Hiring Range $82,950.66 - $136,814.41 GW Staff Approach to Pay How is pay for new employees determined at GW? Healthcare Benefits GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs. II. JOB DETAILS Campus Location: Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C. College/School/Department: Diversity and Inclusion Family Diversity and Inclusion Sub-Family Equal Opportunity Stream Individual Contributor Level Level 4 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Hours Per Week: 40 Work Schedule: M-F Will this job require the employee to work on site? Yes Employee Onsite Status Hybrid Telework: Yes Required Background Check: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Special Instructions to Applicants: Employer will not sponsor for employment Visa status Internal Applicants Only? No Posting Number: S014455 Job Open Date: 09/10/2026 Job Close Date: If temporary, grant funded, Sponsored Project funded or limited term appointment, position funded until: Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently employed with The George Washington University? No Yes * For current GW employees, have you completed your Introductory Employment Period (IEP)?  (As a reminder, employees in their IEP are not eligible to apply for other internal university staff and research positions until the IEP is complete.) Yes, IEP complete No, still in IEP N/a - not a current GW employee * What is your salary range expectation? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/127629": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Law",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Associate Professor of Law Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Associate Professor of Law Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Apply through the AALS Faculty Appointments Register at https://www.aals.org/services/recruitment/ or complete an online faculty application at https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/127573 and upload a cover letter indicating the area of interest with a current curriculum vitae, including a list of references. Please email questions to vkarker@law.gwu.edu . Review of applications will begin on August 13, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications submitted either through AALS or GW’s online system will be considered. Employment offers are contingent on the satisfactory outcome of a standard background screening. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002641 Academic Title: Associate Professor of Law Rank: Associate Professor Administrative Title: Associate Professor of Law Discipline Law Specialty: Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Law School invites applications for two entry-level, tenure-track faculty appointments, beginning in Fall 2027. The school is interested in candidates in two fields of study: immigration and family law. The University and Law School have a strong commitment to preparing students to become resilient leaders who help shape solutions to the pressing challenges of our times. The University and Law School also have a strong commitment to recruiting faculty of the highest caliber who have thrived in different environments and would enrich the university with different experiences and perspectives. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: This position will be responsible for teaching, research, and service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must possess a J.D. degree or an advanced degree in a relevant field, and have relevant experience such as teaching, legal practice, or judicial clerkships. Applicants must also have a strong academic record that demonstrates the potential for superb teaching and show scholarly promise, evidenced by publications in scholarly journals or scholarly works in progress. Advertised Salary: The salary range for these positions is $185,000–$205,000, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Other Benefits: This position qualifies for healthcare and other benefits available to full-time employees. For more information about these benefits, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits. Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Apply through the AALS Faculty Appointments Register at https://www.aals.org/services/recruitment/ or complete an online faculty application at https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/127573 and upload a cover letter indicating the area of interest with a current curriculum vitae, including a list of references. Please email questions to vkarker@law.gwu.edu . Review of applications will begin on August 13, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications submitted either through AALS or GW’s online system will be considered. Employment offers are contingent on the satisfactory outcome of a standard background screening. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/127573 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Interest Statement of Research Interest Sample Publications List of Publications Course Evaluations or Summaries Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you possess a J.D. degree or an advanced degree in a relevant field? Yes No * Do you have a strong academic record that demonstrates the potential for superb teaching? Yes No * Do you have relevant experience such as teaching, legal practice, or judicial clerkship? Yes No * Have you shown scholarly promise, as evidenced by publications in scholarly journals or scholarly works in progress? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120318": {
      "title": "Faculty Position",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Position - General Urology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Position - General Urology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete the online faculty application and upload a CV and cover letter. Review of applications will begin June 20, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002522 Academic Title: Faculty Position - General Urology Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Urology Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates ( MFA ) is seeking a full-time faculty member in the Department of Urology. The MFA is an independent, non-profit clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University. The Department of Urology’s faculty are committed to patient care, cohesive and focused team building, administrative leadership, and resident and medical student education. This non-tenure track position, expected to start as early as Summer 2026, will be at an academic rank (instructor/assistant professor/associate professor/full professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include delivering excellent patient care, teaching residents and medical students, and pursuing scholarly interests consistent with our academic mission. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board certified or board eligible in Urology and have completed an ACGME -accredited residency in Urology at the time of appointment, and be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia, Virginia, and Maryland. Applicants must demonstrate excellence in teaching as evidenced by teaching evaluations, excellence in research as evidenced by scholarly publications or works in progress, and excellence in clinical care as evidenced by experience and professional references. Advertised Salary: $330,000 - $425,000 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete the online faculty application and upload a CV and cover letter. Review of applications will begin June 20, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://gwdocs.com/specialties/urology Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120006 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board certified or board eligible in Urology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you have completed an ACGME- accredited residency in Urology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Are you eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia, Virginia, and Maryland? Yes No * Can you demonstrate excellence in teaching as evidenced by teaching evaluations? Yes No * Can you demonstrate excellence in research as evidenced by scholarly publications or works in progress? Yes No * Can you demonstrate excellence in clinical care as evidenced by experience and professional references? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
