    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120830": {
      "title": "George Washington Employment Site",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Positions - Rheumatology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Positions - Rheumatology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on July 17, 2025, and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002535 Academic Title: Faculty Positions - Rheumatology Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Medicine/Rheumatology Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 9/1/25-6/30/26 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 09/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates ( MFA ) is seeking full-time academic rheumatologists to join the growing Division of Rheumatology of the Department of Medicine. The MFA is an independent, non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University and is part of a large academic health center located in the heart of the nation’s capital. These non-tenure track appointments will be made at a rank (instructor/assistant/associate/full professor) and salary commensurate with experience. These positions are expected to begin as early as Fall 2025. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing quality clinical service, engaging in effective teaching, and maintaining a productive research program. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in Internal Medicine and Rheumatology, and eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. They must also have an established record of providing excellent clinical care services, research productivity, and clinical teaching as demonstrated by experience, publications, evaluations, and/or references. Advertised Salary: $199,000.00 to $249,000.00 Other Benefits: Full benefits package available including professional malpractice coverage (including tail coverage), time off for CME , a Professional Expense Account, retirement benefits, etc. The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on July 17, 2025, and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://smhs.gwu.edu/medicine/divisions/rheumatology Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120403 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board-certified or eligible in Internal Medicine and Rheumatology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do you have an established record of providing excellent clinical care services as demonstrated by experience, publications, evaluations and/or references? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
