    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/123267": {
      "title": "George Washington Employment Site",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Positions in Anesthesiology Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Positions in Anesthesiology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete the online faculty application and upload your CV and cover letter. You will also be asked to provide the names and contact information of three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on January 5, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002576 Academic Title: Faculty Positions in Anesthesiology Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Anesthesiology Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 03/01/2026 - 06/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 03/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates ( MFA ) is seeking to fill full-time faculty positions in the Department of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine to work at the MFA , an independent, non-profit clinical practice group, and/or the Cedar Hill Regional Medical Center, which serves the District of Columbia’s population, mainly in Wards 7 and 8. Regular and limited service faculty appointments to these non-tenure track academic and community-based positions will be made at an academic rank (instructor, assistant professor, associate professor, full professor) and salary commensurate with experience. These positions are expected to begin as early as Spring 2026. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include delivering excellent patient care, participating in administrative duties, teaching learners, and pursuing scholarly interests. Those with subspecialty expertise and/or fellowship training are invited to apply. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board certified in Anesthesiology, or in the certification process, and eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Advertised Salary: $440,000 to $550,000 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete the online faculty application and upload your CV and cover letter. You will also be asked to provide the names and contact information of three references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on January 5, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Department Link: https://smhs.gwu.edu/anesthesiology/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/122845 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board certified in Anesthesiology, or in the certification process at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
