    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/125949": {
      "title": "Endowed Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Endowed Professor of Nursing Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Endowed Professor of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete an online faculty application and upload the following: (1) a cover letter detailing qualifications, teaching and clinical experience, and leadership or administrative experience; and (2) an updated CV. Cover letters should be addressed to Susan Kelly-Weeder, Dean, GW School of Nursing. Please note that all documents related to each section must be combined and uploaded as one single document. Review of applications will begin on July 7, 2025 and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002537 Academic Title: Endowed Professor of Nursing Rank: Professor, Associate Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Nursing Specialty: Contract Type: With Tenure, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 08/01/2025-06/30/2028 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Endowed Professorship in Nursing is responsible for providing support and leadership to the School of Nursing’s ( SON ) academic, research and service missions. A senior-level tenured faculty member, the Endowed Professor is a distinguished scholar with demonstrated success in research, external funding and publications in the areas of health policy, health services and/or nursing workforce research. The Endowed Professor works collaboratively with academic leadership, faculty and staff of the School of Nursing and oversees the Nursing PhD program. This is a full-time 12-month appointment with tenure at the rank of Associate Professor or Full Professor, with a start date as early as fall semester 2025. The Endowed Professor reports to the Associate Dean for Research. All faculty hiring decisions will be contingent upon final approval by the Provost. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include: • Lead and maintain an extramurally funded program of research in health policy, health services research and /or nursing workforce. • Directs PhD in Nursing program • Recruit and mentor PhD students • Teach in area of expertise • Cultivate and lead opportunities for student policy research and initiatives • Strengthen collaborations with external partners with the goal of increasing the impact and dissemination of policy related research • Develops and submits annual reports on the PhD program and overview scholarly productivity of PhD students • Works collaboratively with the Associate Dean for Research and the academic leadership team on the development of early career faculty • Promotes visibility of SON research and scholarship within the school, university, and within local, regional, national and international nursing and healthcare organizations and communities. Minimum Qualifications: • An earned PhD in nursing, public health, public policy or a related field by date of application • Eligible for tenure appointment at the rank of associate or full professor • Demonstrated excellent track record of extramural funding as a Principal Investigator • Experience mentoring doctoral nursing students as well as early career faculty in research and scholarship • Innovative and creative ideas about the future of health policy and related research areas. • Excellent decision-making and problem-solving skills • Evidence of the ability to work and teach in an environment where students, faculty and staff have diverse experiences and perspectives • Strong team leadership and communication skills, excellent interpersonal abilities • Eligibility for RN licensure in the District of Columbia and the Commonwealth of Virginia. Advertised Salary: $150,000 to $190,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for full-time employee health benefits. More information about the benefits that GW offers can be found here: https://hr.gwu.edu/health-benefits Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please complete an online faculty application and upload the following: (1) a cover letter detailing qualifications, teaching and clinical experience, and leadership or administrative experience; and (2) an updated CV. Cover letters should be addressed to Susan Kelly-Weeder, Dean, GW School of Nursing. Please note that all documents related to each section must be combined and uploaded as one single document. Review of applications will begin on July 7, 2025 and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120408 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have an earned PhD in nursing, public health, public policy or related field by date of application? Yes No * Are you eligible for tenure appointment at the rank of associate or full professor? Yes No * Can you demonstrate an excellent track record of extramural funding as a Principal Investigator? Yes No * Do you have experience mentoring doctoral nursing students as well as early career faculty in research and scholarship? Yes No * Do you have innovative and creative ideas about the future of health policy and related research areas? Yes No * Do you have excellent decision-making and problem-solving skills? Yes No * Can you demonstrate evidence of the ability to work and teach in an environment where students, faculty and staff have diverse experiences and perspectives? Yes No * Do you have strong team leadership, communication skills and excellent interpersonal abilities? Yes No * Are you eligible for RN licensure in the District of Columbia and Virginia? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/118861": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Nephrology)",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Nephrology) Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Nephrology) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on March 26, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002496 Academic Title: Open Rank Faculty Position in Medicine (Nephrology) Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Nephrology Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 7/1/2025-6/30/2026 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2025 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates, an independent non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with the George Washington University, seeks full-time academic nephrologists for its Division of Kidney Diseases & Hypertension in the Department of Medicine. These non-tenure track appointments will be made at a rank (Instructor/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) and salary commensurate with experience, with the possibility of additional incentives if eligible. The Division of Kidney Diseases and Hypertension at the George Washington University School of Medicine has a long and distinguished history of remarkable achievements in scientific discovery, education, and clinical care of kidney disease. The division is ranked by the US News and World Report, and it has several NIH -funded faculty members. These positions are expected to begin as early as July 1, 2025. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing excellent clinical care, maintaining an active research program, and participating in clinical teaching. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board certified/eligible in Nephrology and eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. A record of academic excellence, as demonstrated by clinical experience, publications, evaluations, and/or references, is required. Advertised Salary: $240,000.00 to $265,000 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits. Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Review of applications will begin on March 26, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://smhs.gwu.edu/medicine/divisions/renal Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/118117 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board certified/eligible in Nephrology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do you have a record of academic excellence, as demonstrated by clinical experience, publications, evaluations and/or references? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128816": {
      "title": "George Washington Employment Site",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Positions in Emergency Medicine Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Positions in Emergency Medicine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Complete the online faculty application and upload a CV and cover letter. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002656 Academic Title: Faculty Positions in Emergency Medicine Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Emergency Medicine Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 10/1/2026-6/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 10/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: Academic Emergency Medicine Partners, an independent academic clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University, seeks full-time academic emergency medicine physicians. The Department of Emergency Medicine provides staffing for the emergency units at George Washington University Hospital, the Walter Reed National Military Medical Center, and the Washington, DC, Veterans Administration Medical Center. The Department’s educational programs include a four-year residency and ten fellowship programs. These non-tenure-track appointments, expected to start as early as October 2026, will be made at a rank (instructor/assistant/associate/full professor) and a salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing clinical and consultative service, teaching fellows, residents, and medical students, and maintaining an active research program. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be American Board of Emergency Medicine or American Osteopathic Board of Emergency Medicine certified or have completed a residency certified by the Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education or American Osteopathic Association at the time of appointment. They must also be eligible for licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Advertised Salary: Commensurate with experience ranging from $275,000 to $325,000. Other Benefits: The AEMP also provides generous health and other benefits; details can be found at https://www.ies.healthcare/job/gw-faculty-em/#job-details . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Complete the online faculty application and upload a CV and cover letter. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://www.ies.healthcare/services/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128454 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be American Board of Emergency Medicine or American Osteopathic Board of Emergency Medicine certified or have completed a residency certified by the Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education or American Osteopathic Association at the time of appointment? Yes No * Are you or will you be eligible for District of Columbia Medical Licensure at the time of employment? Yes No * Was your residency a three or four year program? (Open Ended Question) * Do you speak a foreign language?  Which one(s)? (Open Ended Question) Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/124379": {
      "title": "George Washington Employment Site",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Faculty Positions in Radiology – Academic Radiologists Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Faculty Positions in Radiology – Academic Radiologists Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online application and upload a CV and cover letter describing your background and academic interests. Review of applications will begin March 23, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002586 Academic Title: Faculty Positions in Radiology – Academic Radiologists Rank: Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Administrative Title: Academic Abdominal Imager - Radiology Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: Radiology Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 05/01/2026-06/30/2027 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 05/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates ( MFA ) Department of Radiology is seeking academic radiologists to join our faculty as we expand our practice. The MFA is an independent, non-profit, academic clinical practice group strategically aligned with The George Washington University. These non-tenure-track, full-time appointments, expected to start as early as Spring 2026, will be made at an academic rank (instructor, assistant professor, associate professor, or professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include interpreting radiologic imaging and diagnostic studies in fluoroscopy, body CT, ultrasound, MRI , musculoskeletal imaging, or neuroradiology. Additional duties include teaching medical students, residents, and fellows; participating in multidisciplinary clinical research; collaborating with referring clinical colleagues and administrative partners; and assisting with departmental administrative functions. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be board-certified or eligible in radiology, have completed a fellowship, and be eligible for medical licensure in the District of Columbia by the time of appointment. Advertised Salary: $438,974 to $512,915 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits, details of which can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online application and upload a CV and cover letter describing your background and academic interests. Review of applications will begin March 23, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://gwdocs.com/specialties/radiology Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/124135 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be board-certified or eligible in radiology at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you have completed a fellowship at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be eligible for medical licensure in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
