    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128823": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Economics Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Economics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application procedure: Please complete an online faculty application at the AEA Job Portal ( https://www.aeaweb.org/joe/ ). Applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest detailing the position for which you are applying, (2) a current CV, (3) one or at most two research papers, (4) a statement of your research and teaching interests and qualifications, (5) teaching evaluations (if available), (6) syllabi of courses taught (if available), (7) arrange for three letters of reference to be submitted. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin October 17, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The application deadline is December 15, 2026. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002657 Academic Title: Assistant Professor of Economics Rank: Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Social Sciences Specialty: Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University’s Department of Economics invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position beginning as early as Fall 2027. We seek applicants specializing in applied microeconomics who demonstrate strong potential for scholarly achievement and excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be expected to maintain an active research program and contribute to the intellectual and professional life of the Department and University. Teaching responsibilities will include courses for undergraduate and graduate students in the Economics Department. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in economics with a primary focus on applied microeconomics. Applicants must have a Ph.D. or complete all requirements for the Ph.D. by the date of appointment. Advertised Salary: $140,000-$155,000 Other Benefits: Health Benefits: GW offers a comprehensive benefit package that includes medical, dental, vision, life & disability insurance, time off & leave, retirement savings, tuition, well-being and various voluntary benefits. For program details and eligibility, please visit https://hr.gwu.edu/benefits-programs . Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: Application procedure: Please complete an online faculty application at the AEA Job Portal ( https://www.aeaweb.org/joe/ ). Applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest detailing the position for which you are applying, (2) a current CV, (3) one or at most two research papers, (4) a statement of your research and teaching interests and qualifications, (5) teaching evaluations (if available), (6) syllabi of courses taught (if available), (7) arrange for three letters of reference to be submitted. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin October 17, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The application deadline is December 15, 2026. Department Link: https://economics.columbian.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128624 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
