    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128674": {
      "title": "George Washington Employment Site",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. When applying for the Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences position please highlight the experiences you have that address the job responsibilities and demonstrate your ability to thrive in this position and within the broader GWLAI and university communities. To be considered, please complete an online application and upload a CV and a cover letter that includes an assessment of skills and experiences related to minimum and preferred qualifications. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on October 12, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Employment offers are contingent upon the satisfactory outcome of a reference check and standard background screening. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002653 Academic Title: Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences Rank: Librarian I, Librarian II, Librarian III, Librarian IV Administrative Title: Discipline Libraries Specialty: Contract Type: Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - Renewable period depending on rank at date of hire. Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search Proposed Start Date: 10/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Libraries and Academic Innovation ( GWLAI ) enriches the academic experience of scholars and students and sparks innovation at GW. We enable research and teaching through access to the latest scholarship and rich archival resources, tailored support for researchers at all levels, guidance for faculty who want to explore new teaching methods and technologies in the classroom, and robust support for online education. Through innovative partnerships, dynamic workshops, and team-based approaches to project management and problem solving, GWLAI fosters collaboration and provides leadership across the university to support the shared mission of generating, making accessible, and preserving new knowledge. Having joined the Association of American Universities ( AAU ) in 2023, and guided by a new Strategic Framework , GW is at an exciting moment in its history and trajectory, and GWLAI is a key partner in supporting the university’s research and scholarly advancements and promoting discoveries and innovations made by the research community. GWLAI seeks a collaborative and service-oriented Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences to join the Research and User Services ( RUS ) department. RUS is a highly collaborative unit where librarians work together and share responsibility for meeting the full range of student, faculty, and researcher needs across disciplines. This position plays a vital role in supporting interdisciplinary teaching, research, and publishing across the Social and Political Sciences with an emphasis on international affairs, political science, public policy, economics, and related fields. As an active member of the RUS team, the incumbent also provides research support, instruction, and collection development services to all areas of the university, including the First Year Writing program. GWLAI staff and librarians are champions of open access and support open scholarly communication and publishing practices, including the adoption and creation of open educational resources ( OER ). Librarians contribute to the scholarly community through research, professional engagement, and service. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Support the research and instructional needs of faculty, students, and researchers in the Social and Political Sciences, with an emphasis on international affairs, political science, public policy, economics, and related fields. Conduct library instruction for undergraduate and graduate level courses in partnership with faculty, including partnering with GW’s first-year University Writing Program. Provide research consultations and services (chat, email) across disciplines. Participate in collaborative collection development and relationship-building with departments and research units to understand and meet their evolving needs. Provide expert guidance on Social Science research methods, statistical data analysis, visualization and use, text and data mining, and/or other quantitative and qualitative research methods. Contribute to strategic initiatives or teams within GWLAI , including efforts related to scholarly communication, open access publishing, open education, research impact and visibility, and/or data literacy and computational fluency. Minimum Qualifications: ALA -accredited Master’s degree in library and information science OR other advanced degree with relevant experience by date of appointment. Demonstrated collaboration skills and a commitment to supporting an inclusive and equitable research community. Strong initiative and a results-driven approach in previous roles Excellent oral and written communication skills. Awareness of current scholarly communication and research trends, issues, and challenges facing researchers in an academic environment. Experience or demonstrated potential to support Social Science research methods and publishing practices. Advertised Salary: Librarian 1: $58,566 - $65,000; Librarian 2: $61,156 - $78,000; Librarian 3: $65,156 - $81,000; Librarian 4: $71,656 - $130,000 Other Benefits: Salary and appointment at the rank of Librarian I/II/ III /IV are dependent upon qualifications. Salary is negotiable, contingent upon rank, skills and qualifications and is competitive for DC area academic libraries. Comprehensive benefits package includes 22 days/year paid annual leave; 12 days/year paid sick leave; paid winter break and 8 other holidays; medical, dental, and vision; 401(A) retirement plan, 4% base and GW will match 150% of the first 4% of your 403(B) contributions, up to a maximum of 6% of your eligible compensation; tuition assistance; ongoing support for professional development; and paid parental leave. Librarians are eligible to apply for research leave after a defined period of service. For benefit details, please visit GW Benefits . This position is classified as a Council of Librarians position and is eligible for a hybrid on-campus/remote work schedule. This position is a continual reappointment position with reappointment periods of 3-5 years depending on rank. Proven commitment to the profession is expected and can be exhibited through service, publication, and/or presentations. Other Information: PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge of, or experience working with, financial and economic data. A strong understanding of the research lifecycle, scholarly communication, and academic publishing. A robust understanding of computational and data research methods, statistical data analysis and use methods, text and data mining, or other quantitative and qualitative research methods. Experience with GIS , coding, data visualization, or computational research tools. We recognize that strong candidates may not meet every qualification. If you are passionate about this role, we encourage you to apply and highlight how your experiences align with the position. This position reports to a Director of Research Services and is eligible for partial telework. The University and GWLAI have a strong commitment to recruiting librarians of the highest caliber who have thrived in different environments and would enrich the University with different experiences and perspectives. We offer a work environment that values and supports collaboration, teamwork, and professional growth and development. A virtual information session for interested candidates will be offered in the coming weeks. Please visit https://go.gwu.edu/librarianjobs for details. Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying for the Research Services Librarian for the Social and Political Sciences position please highlight the experiences you have that address the job responsibilities and demonstrate your ability to thrive in this position and within the broader GWLAI and university communities. To be considered, please complete an online application and upload a CV and a cover letter that includes an assessment of skills and experiences related to minimum and preferred qualifications. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will begin on October 12, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Employment offers are contingent upon the satisfactory outcome of a reference check and standard background screening. Department Link: http://library.gwu.edu/ Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128316 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Resume Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have an ALA-accredited Master’s degree in library and information science OR other advanced degree with relevant experience by date of appointment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated collaboration skills and a commitment to supporting an inclusive and equitable research community? Yes No * Do you have a strong initiative and a results-driven approach in previous roles? Yes No * Can you demonstrate excellent oral and written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have awareness of current scholarly communication and research trends, issues, and\nchallenges facing researchers in an academic environment? Yes No * Do you have experience or demonstrated potential to support Social Science research methods and\npublishing practices? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/124808": {
      "title": "George Washington Employment Site",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, including a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Application review will begin on April 20, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002563 Academic Title: Open Rank Faculty Positions in Outpatient Primary Care Rank: Assistant Professor, Instructor, Professor, Associate Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Clinical Medicine-MD Specialty: General Internal Medicine Contract Type: Non-Tenure Track, Renewable Appointment (initial appt period) - 07/01/26-06/30/27 Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 07/01/2026 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The George Washington University Medical Faculty Associates, an independent non-profit academic clinical practice group affiliated with The George Washington University, seeks full-time academic physicians to join our Division of Primary Care in the Department of Medicine. Join a collaborative and mission-driven team of clinician-educators in downtown Washington, DC. These positions offer a unique opportunity to engage in clinical care and medical education. These non-tenure-track faculty appointments, expected to start as early as July 2026, will be made at a rank (Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor) and salary commensurate with experience. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include providing direct, high-quality patient care in an outpatient setting; engaging in population health management and quality/safety initiatives; participating in administrative duties; and contributing to the teaching and mentorship of medical students, interns, residents, fellows, and other learners. All faculty are encouraged to develop scholarly interests and are expected to collaborate with the larger team to enhance access, reduce costs, improve quality, and promote better health outcomes. Faculty can receive up to 10% protected time for research in the first year. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must be ABIM -certified or eligible and licensed in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment. Applicants must also have a record of providing high-quality, high-value, evidence-based, and team-oriented patient care, outstanding teaching, and scholarly productivity, with a dedication to professional growth. Advertised Salary: $170,000.00 - $220,000.00 Other Benefits: The MFA also provides generous health and other benefits; details can be found at https://careers.gwdocs.com/benefits. Other Information: Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please complete an online faculty application, including a curriculum vitae and cover letter. Application review will begin on April 20, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Department Link: https://medicine.smhs.gwu.edu/general-internal-medicine Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/120140 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you be ABIM-certified or eligible at the time of appointment? Yes No * Will you be licensed in the District of Columbia at the time of appointment? Yes No * Do have a record of providing high-quality, high-value, evidence-based, and team-oriented patient care, outstanding teaching, and scholarly productivity, with a dedication to professional growth? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128943": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Information Systems and Technology Management",
      "description": "George Washington Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Information Systems and Technology Management Skip to Main Content SEARCH JOBS Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Job Libraries Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Information Systems and Technology Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, job market paper (additional papers welcome), research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for three references. Letters of recommendation may be requested at a later stage of the selection process. Only complete applications will be considered. We encourage candidates to apply early to ensure full and timely consideration. ISTM faculty expect to conduct initial interviews with selected candidates at CIST 2026 in San Francisco, CA, and at ICIS 2026 in Lisbon, Portugal . If you have any questions regarding the position, please contact Dr. Wenjing Duan (wduan@gwu.edu). Review of applications will begin October 26, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Recruitment Plan I. RECRUITMENT PLAN Posting Number: F002661 Academic Title: Assistant Professor of Information Systems and Technology Management Rank: Assistant Professor Administrative Title: Discipline Business Specialty: Contract Type: Tenure Track Required Licenses/Certifications and other Specific Requirements: Criminal History Screening, Education/Degree/Certifications Verification, Social Security Number Trace, and Sex Offender Registry Search, Prior Employment Verification, This position requires a licensure, certification, or special requirements Proposed Start Date: 08/01/2027 Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Position Description Summary: The Department of Information Systems and Technology Management at the George Washington University School of Business invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Information Systems position beginning in Fall 2027. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and an established research record. Applicants are expected to develop and sustain a high-quality research program leading to publications in premier scholarly journals. Teaching responsibilities will include high-quality courses for undergraduate and graduate students in the School of Business. Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching excellence and flexibility in contributing to the Department’s evolving teaching needs in artificial intelligence, information systems, technology management, and emerging digital technologies. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: This position is part of a broader GWSB cluster hire in Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Analytics, which includes faculty positions in Information Systems and Technology Management, Decision Sciences, and Finance. Within this broader initiative, the ISTM Department seeks candidates whose research examines important technological, organizational, economic, or societal questions related to artificial intelligence, digital innovation, and emerging digital technologies. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, generative AI, human-AI interaction, responsible AI, AI-enabled innovation and transformation, and the economic and societal implications of AI. The position is grounded in the Information Systems discipline while encouraging interdisciplinary collaboration across GWSB . The Information Systems and Technology Management Department offers a collaborative research environment with faculty interests spanning AI, digital platforms and markets, emerging technologies, organizational agility through IT, e-business, and innovation and entrepreneurship. The Department offers undergraduate and graduate programs in information systems and technology management and contributes to GWSB’s growing portfolio of AI-focused programs, including the M.S. in Artificial Intelligence for Business ( MSAIB ). Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Computer Science, Engineering, Business, or a closely related field, completed or expected to be completed by the date of appointment. Candidates must demonstrate strong potential for research excellence and publication in premier scholarly journals in Information Systems or closely related disciplines, as well as potential for teaching excellence at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Advertised Salary: $190,000 - $205,000 Other Benefits: This position is eligible for full-time health benefits.  For more information, please visit: https://hr.gwu.edu/health-benefits. Other Information: Located in the heart of Washington, D.C., the George Washington University offers a distinctive setting for technology research. Faculty benefit from proximity to and opportunities for interaction with researchers, economists, policymakers, international organizations, federal agencies, industry, and a growing technology and innovation ecosystem. Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, job market paper (additional papers welcome), research statement, teaching statement, and contact information for three references. Letters of recommendation may be requested at a later stage of the selection process. Only complete applications will be considered. We encourage candidates to apply early to ensure full and timely consideration. ISTM faculty expect to conduct initial interviews with selected candidates at CIST 2026 in San Francisco, CA, and at ICIS 2026 in Lisbon, Portugal . If you have any questions regarding the position, please contact Dr. Wenjing Duan (wduan@gwu.edu). Review of applications will begin October 26, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Department Link: https://business.gwu.edu/about/departments/information-systems-technology-management Posting Close Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Background Screening Successful Completion of a Background Screening will be required as a condition of hire. EEO Statement: The university is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer that does not unlawfully discriminate in any of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or on any other basis prohibited by applicable law. Quick Link https://www.gwu.jobs/postings/128790 Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Names and Contact Information for References Other Documents Refer to Special Instructions to Applicants Statement of Teaching and Research Interest Optional Documents List of Publications Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have a Ph.D. in Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Computer Science, Engineering, Business, or a closely related field, completed or expected to be completed by the date of appointment? Yes No * Can you demonstrate strong potential for research excellence and publication in premier scholarly journals in Information Systems or closely related disciplines Yes No * Can you demonstrate potential for teaching excellence at the undergraduate and graduate levels? Yes No Human Resource Management & Development 2013 H Street, NW, 3rd Floor Washington, DC 20006 Phone: 202-994-8500 Fax: 202-994-9680 Email: askhrmd@gwu.edu Recognition_Toolkit Talent@GWLogin Privacy Notice Connect with us To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
